  "raw_text": "241\n\nLilia takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto rejoice, to be glad, to be entertained, to have fun, to become happy, to become joyful\n \n/\nregocijarse, alegrarse, entretenerse, divertirse, volverse feliz, volverse alegre\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-10/19\n):\n \nYawan nahki lilia taki ba, nahki sip sa Gâd mayunra lâka ba pain apia kaka saura takaia?\n \n–\n \n(With\nregards to) how we are being entertained, how is it able to become good or bad for our worship?\n \n/ (Con respecto a) cómo\nnos estamos entreteniendo, ¿cómo puede ser bueno o malo para nuestra adoración?)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb235\n):\n \nPal G\nâ\nd ra tingki win bara lilia takan\n \n–\n \nPaul said thanks to God and rejoiced\n \n/ Pablo dijo gracias a Dios y se\nregocijó)\n\nLilia takaia dukya nani\n \n–\n \nentertainment\n \n/ entretenimiento\n\nLin takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto borrow\n \n/ pedir prestado\n\nMarit takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto get married\n \n/ casarse\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf-5\n):\n \nUpla nani ba marit taki piua ba wina “w\nâl ba ai wîna kumi\n \nbaku” takisa\n \n–\n \nFrom the time that people are\ngetting\n \nmarried, they become “the two like just one flesh”\n \n/ Desde el momento en que las personas se casan, se\nconvierten en \"los dos como una sola carne\")\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-05/21\n):\n \nupla lalukra kum wal baman marit takaia\n \n–\n \nto get married only with a believer\n \n(“only in the Lord”\n-\nnwt-\n1Kor7:39\n)\n \n/ casarse solo con un/una creyente (“solo en el Se\nñ\nor”\n-\ntnm-1Kor7:39\n))\n\nMarit taki yua liliaka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nmarriage celebration, marriage reception\n \n/ celebración de matrimonio,\nrecepción de matrimonio\n\nMarit takras rug takaia lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nfornication\n \n/ fornicación\n\nMiks takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become mixed\n \n/ mezclarse\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-11/18\n):\n \n..., kristian kangrigisan ba miks takan.\n \n–\n \n..., the Christian congregation became mixed (more diverse).\n \n/\n..., la congregación cristiana se volvió mixta (más diversa).)\n\nMistik takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto make a mistake\n \n/ cometer un error\n\nMistik tatakra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nperson who makes mistakes, imperfect person\n \n/ persona que comete\nerrores, persona imperfecta\n\nNu takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto come to know, to determine, to perceive\n \n/ llegar a conocer, llegar a saber, determinar, percibir\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-06/19\n):\n \nNahki sip sa piu bani kau pain nu takaia Jehova dîa want sa yawan dukiara?\n \n–\n \nHow are we able to\nalways be coming to know/perceive better what Jehovah wants for us?\n \n/ ¿Cómo podemos llegar a saber/percibir mejor lo\nque Jehová quiere para nosotros?)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nth-19\n):\n \nSip sa kaka, makabi walanka nani upla ra dauks witin dîa luki ba nu takaia dukiara.\n \n–\n \nIf possible, ask the\nperson questions in order to come to know what he/she is thinking.\n \n/ Si es posible, hágale preguntas a la persona para\nsaber qué está pensando.)\n\nKau nu takaia\n \n–\n \nto come to know more\n \n/\n \nllegar\n \na saber más\n,\n \nllegar\n \na conocer\n \nmás\n\nNu takaia daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto cause to want to know, to arouse curiosity\n \n/ hacer querer saber, despertar la\ncuriosidad\n\nPah takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto appear\n \n/ aparecer\n\n(Ex/Ej(\n2 Sam 18:9\n):\n \nDebit suliarka (Absalón) mawan kat pah takan\n \n–\n \nDavid’s soldiers appeared in front of Absalom\n \n/ Los\nsoldados de David aparecieron frente a Absalón)\n\nPâna takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become friends\n \n/ hacerse amigos\n\n(Ex/Ej(\njl6\n):\n \nWan aikuki pana takaia\n \n–\n \nto become friends with us\n \n/ hacerse amigo de nosotros)\n\nParam takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become clear, to become visible, to become open, to become manifest, to appear\n \n/ hacerse\nclaro, hacerse visible, abrirse, manifestarse, aparecer\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-11/18\n):\n \nJisas pruan wina buan piua ra param takan Pita bara disaipil wala nani ra.\n \n–\n \nWhen Jesus was\nresurrected, he appeared to Peter and other disciples.\n \n/ Cuando Jesús resucitó, se le apareció a Pedro y a otros discípulos.)\n\nPraut takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become angry, to get angry, to become vexed\n \n/ enojarse\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf-23\n):\n \nLuhpiam ba dîa dîa mai aisabia sin, witin bîla dakpara bara praut takpara\n \n–\n \nRegardless of what your child\nsays to you, do not interrupt them and do not get angry\n \n/ Independientemente de lo que le diga su hijo, no lo interrumpa\ny no se enoje)\n\nPri takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become free, to become liberated\n \n/ volverse libre, liberarse\n\nRidi takaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nRedi takaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto become prepared, to come to be prepared, to get ready\n \n/ estar preparado,\nvenir a estar preparado, prepararse\n\nPain ridi takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto prepare well\n \n/ prepararse bien\n\nRidi takaia\n \nwauhkataya\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nworkbook\n \n/ libro de trabajo\n\nRidi takanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npreparation\n \n/ preparación\n\nRidi takan lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npreparedness, readiness, preparation\n \n/ preparación, disposición",
